          ],
          "content": "Angles Formed: $\\angle  AEF , \\angle  BEF , \\angle  DFE , \\angle  CFE$ Here $\\angle  AEF$ & ∠CFE are larger than ∠BEF & ∠DFE Try more cases by folding rectangular sheets in different ways."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.348,
            0.6,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": "**Q.2. In each case, determine which angle is greater and why.** a. $\\angle \\mathrm{AOB}   or   \\angle \\mathrm{XOY}$ b. $\\angle \\mathbf{AOB}   or   \\angle \\mathbf{XOB}$ c. ∠**XOB** or ∠**XOC**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.452,
            0.727,
            0.546
          ],
          "content": "**Discuss with your friends on how you decided which one is greater.** Ans. (a)- $\\angle  AOB ; \\angle  XOY$ is an acute angle and $\\angle AOB = \\angle AOX + \\angle XOY + \\angle YOB$ (b)- $\\angle \\mathrm { A O B }$ (c) – $- \\mathrm{None} . \\angle \\mathrm{XOB} = \\angle \\mathrm{XOC}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.581,
            0.602,
            0.597
          ],
          "content": "**Q.3. Which angle is greater:** ∠**XOY or** ∠**AOB? Give reasons.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.607,
            0.836,
            0.623
          ],
          "content": "Ans. By looking at the figure we cannot say. Superimposition or measurement is necessary here."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.659,
            0.218,
            0.675
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Section 2.8"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.686,
            0.192,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "**Page 28**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.709,
            0.881,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": "**Q. Is it possible to draw** $\\overset { \\rightarrow } { \\mathbf { o c } }$ **such that the two angles are equal to each other in size?** Ans. Yes, when $\\overrightarrow { \\mathrm { O A } }$ and $\\overrightarrow { \\mathbf { O B } }$ overlap each other on folding the Vidya’s notebook, the crease OC will divide $\\angle \\mathbf { A O B }$ in two equal sized angles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.811,
            0.186,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": "**Page 29**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.837,
            0.881,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": "**Q. If a straight angle is formed by half of a full turn, how much of a full turn will form a right angle?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.878,
            0.304,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "Ans. ${ \\frac { 1 } { 4 } }   \\mathrm { o f }$ a full turn."
